abstract: "A curated, standardized collection of empirical phylogenetic datasets covering taxonomic groups across Bacteria, Archaea, and Eukaryota. Organized into 62 partitions yielding 264 standardized trees (218 Condamine family-level + 25 further partition-canonical + 21 sub-clade/reference), with tip-label normalized Newick trees, a global standardized-label dictionary, full label mappings, and metadata. The TimeTree-of-Life (Hedges et al. 2015) is cited as a cross-cutting reference but is not redistributed in this deposit, at the TimeTree project's request (available from timetree.org). Companion to the manuscript 'Where the tree of life is empirically resolved, and where it is not: an open atlas of species-level phylogenies and their archival uncertainty' (Richter, 2026, under review)."
